@startsalt
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: every frame the topology strip can draw, per backend, and what each element means
' covers: internal/run/topology.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/topology.go
'   the mechanism behind it .... _spec/internal/choiceui/topology-strip.puml
'   scrolling, panes: unbuilt .. _spec/_plans/choiceui-viewport-proposals.puml
'   the form it hangs under .... _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml
'   help pinned last, grows .... _spec/internal/choiceui/choice-prompt-render.puml
'   THE SBX AXIS ............... _spec/internal/sbx/policy-baseline.puml
'   what the Kit allowlists ..... internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go Spec()
'   the key on sbx ............. _spec/internal/sbx/credential-path.puml
'   the docker tiers ........... _spec/internal/egress/egress-tiers.puml
'   who the '?' actually asks .. _spec/internal/reviewgate/pty-review-proxy.puml
'   the key on docker .......... _spec/_paradigms/credential-boundary.puml
'
' THE CORRECTION THIS FILE EXISTS TO CARRY: there is no single egress axis. The
' picker shows sbx's host BASELINE on a sbx harness and proveo's TIERS on a docker
' one, and the two are different questions with different answers and a different
' hop behind them. An earlier draft glossed allow-all/balanced/deny-all as nicer
' names for open/allowlist/review; they are a separate, host-wide axis that proveo
' reports and never sets. Every frame below therefore names its backend.
'
'
' THE GLYPHS BELOW ARE THE DIAGRAM'S, NOT THE TERMINAL'S. Emoji read well here and
' badly in a grid: the speaking head is two runes that go-runewidth measures as one
' column and terminals draw as two, and the cloud is ambiguous-width. The strip
' therefore ships with Nerd Font devicons (one rune, one column) and an ASCII tier,
' and PROVEO_GLYPHS=off draws the ASCII figure rather than none. Read every emoji
' below as "the key", "the cloud", "the bubble" — a role, not a codepoint.
'
' Salt has no conditional construct, so every state is a separate frame. Lanes use
' '-' and '=' because the diagram font carries no box-drawing set — which makes
' these sheets a literal picture of the PROVEO_GLYPHS=ascii tier.
title The topology strip in every selectable state, on both backends

{
{^"Anatomy — six columns, three rows, one caption. Nothing here ever moves."
  . | . | . | . | . | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  () host | ══▸ | [ <:speech_balloon:> claudecode ] | ══▸ | () egress <:key:> | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  ▴ | ◂── | () interface ↑ | . | . | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  the caption — the same four facts as the figure, in one sentence
  .
  **() host** your machine · **the square** the container the agent runs in ·
  **() interface** what it drives, hanging off the square and returning to you ·
  **() egress** the hop, whoever owns it · **<:cloud:>** one per surviving lane
}
..
{^"Which axis you are on is decided by the harness, not by the operator"
{#
  backend | harnesses | the egress row shows | the hop in the strip is | the row is
  **sbx** | claudecode · cursor | allow-all · balanced · deny-all | sbx's own proxy; the Kit allowlist rides on top | **LOCKED** — reported, never set
  **docker** | opencode · cecli | open · allowlist · review | proveo's mitmproxy, plus Squid on the enforced tiers | a choice
}
  .
  The sandbox add-on is now compulsory, so a harness that declares sbx is ALWAYS
  on the first row and never sees a tier. The docker row is reached by declaring
  dind, or on a sbx harness by PROVEO_SBX=0 or --egress-mode review.
  .
  On sbx the baseline is host-wide and shared by sandboxes proveo never started,
  which is why the row is locked. The strip is REPORTING there — it draws a fact
  about the machine, and its caption carries the change hint, not a choice.
  .
  **deny-all is the tightest posture, NOT a dead one.** It is classified by the
  ABSENCE of a network allow rule, not by an explicit deny — and the Kit can only
  add allows, never subtract. So the Kit's list is the only one standing, and it
  is built from the harness's declared hosts plus the API hosts of the providers
  proveo actually detected. The agent reaches its model, and nothing else.
  .
  That is also why the lane count falls 3 -> 2 -> 1 across the row rather than
  3 -> 2 -> 0: the axis runs riskier to safer, and the safest end still has to
  let the run work. A frame with no lane at all would say the agent cannot think.
}
..
{^"Variant S · the sbx backend — the baseline, and sbx as the broker"
{
{^"allow-all · broker"
  . | . | . | . | . | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  () host | ══▸ | [ <:speech_balloon:> claudecode ] | ══▸ | () sbx proxy <:key:> | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  ▴ | ◂── | () interface ↑ | . | . | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  allow-all — everything is reachable, so the Kit ADDS reach instead of limiting it
}
{^"allow-all · forward"
  . | . | . | . | . | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  () host | ══▸ | [ <:key:> <:speech_balloon:> claudecode ] | ══▸ | () sbx proxy | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  ▴ | ◂── | () interface ↑ | . | . | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  allow-all · forward — a bare -e NAME: the agent process holds the real value
}
}
{
{^"balanced · broker"
  . | . | . | ───▸ | . | ───▸ <:cloud:>
  () host | ══▸ | [ <:speech_balloon:> claudecode ] | ───▸ | () sbx proxy <:key:> | ───▸ <:cloud:>
  ▴ | ◂── | () interface ↑ | ───▸ | . | ───×
  balanced — the host's own allows, plus proveo's; sbx injects the key
}
{^"balanced · forward"
  . | . | . | ───▸ | . | ───▸ <:cloud:>
  () host | ══▸ | [ <:key:> <:speech_balloon:> claudecode ] | ───▸ | () sbx proxy | ───▸ <:cloud:>
  ▴ | ◂── | () interface ↑ | ───▸ | . | ───×
  balanced · forward — the host's allows plus proveo's; the value is inside
}
}
{
{^"deny-all · broker — the Kit lane survives, and it is the only one that does"
  . | . | . | ───▸ | . | ───▸ <:cloud:> the provider
  () host | ══▸ | [ <:speech_balloon:> claudecode ] | ───▸ | () sbx proxy <:key:> | ──×
  ▴ | ◂── | () interface ↑ | ───▸ | . | ──×
  deny-all — only the Kit allowlist gets out: your provider, and nothing else
}
{^"deny-all · forward"
  . | . | . | ───▸ | . | ───▸ <:cloud:> the provider
  () host | ══▸ | [ <:key:> <:speech_balloon:> claudecode ] | ───▸ | () sbx proxy | ──×
  ▴ | ◂── | () interface ↑ | ───▸ | . | ──×
  deny-all · forward — one lane out, and the real key rides inside the square
}
}
  .
  'broker' names a different party here than it does on docker: there is no
  proveo egress layer at all, so proveo steps aside and SBX brokers — the value
  never reaches the agent either way, but the hop in the picture is sbx's.
  .
  cursor declares credentials [forward] alone, so its credentials row has one
  option and applicableRows drops it. On cursor only the left column exists, and
  the key is inside the square on every frame.
}
..
{^"Variant D · the docker backend — proveo's tiers, and proveo's mitmproxy"
{
{^"open · broker"
  . | . | . | . | . | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  () host | ══▸ | [ <:speech_balloon:> opencode ] | ══▸ | () mitm <:key:> | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  ▴ | ◂── | () interface ↑ | . | . | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  open — the MITM is still in the path; only the allowlist and the budget are off
}
{^"open · forward — the deliberate bypass, and the only frame with no hop"
  . | . | . | . | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  () host | ══▸ | [ <:key:> <:speech_balloon:> opencode ] | ═══════▸ | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  ▴ | ◂── | () interface ↑ | . | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  **open · forward — BYPASS: no MITM at all, and the real key in the container**
}
}
{
{^"allowlist · broker"
  . | . | . | ───▸ | . | ───▸ <:cloud:>
  () host | ══▸ | [ <:speech_balloon:> opencode ] | ───▸ | () mitm + squid <:key:> | ───▸ <:cloud:>
  ▴ | ◂── | () interface ↑ | ───▸ | . | ───×
  allowlist — screened at the hop, the unlisted refused; the key never goes inside
}
{^"allowlist · forward"
  . | . | . | ───▸ | . | ───▸ <:cloud:>
  () host | ══▸ | [ <:key:> <:speech_balloon:> opencode ] | ───▸ | () mitm + squid | ───▸ <:cloud:>
  ▴ | ◂── | () interface ↑ | ───▸ | . | ───×
  allowlist · forward — screened at the hop; the real key rides inside the square
}
}
{
{^"review · broker — the '?' comes back to YOU, which is what makes it review"
  **?** ▴ | ◂─ ─ ─ | ◂─ ─ ─ | ◂─ ─ ─ | **?** the hop asks | .
  () host | ══▸ | [ <:speech_balloon:> opencode ] | ══▸ | () mitm + squid <:key:> | <:cloud:>
  ▴ | ◂── | () interface ↑ | . | . | .
  review — 'Allow connection to <host>?' over your suspended agent TUI
}
{^"review · forward"
  **?** ▴ | ◂─ ─ ─ | ◂─ ─ ─ | ◂─ ─ ─ | **?** the hop asks | .
  () host | ══▸ | [ <:key:> <:speech_balloon:> opencode ] | ══▸ | () mitm + squid | <:cloud:>
  ▴ | ◂── | () interface ↑ | . | . | .
  review · forward — you answer each host; the key is inside regardless
}
}
  .
  **Drawing review with no lanes is a licence, not a measurement.** Its sidecars
  are byte-for-byte allowlist's — only PROVEO_EGRESS_REVIEW=1 differs — so the
  empty lanes say 'nothing has been consented YET', not 'nothing is wired'.
  .
  'open · forward' is the one cell with no hop to draw: buildOpen returns a bridge
  network with no MITM the moment credentials are forwarded. Add --local-model
  without host Ollama and it builds a network plus an Ollama sidecar — still no hop.
}
..
{^"...times agent evidence, which swaps one glyph and changes nothing else"
{
{^"default"
  () host | ══▸ | [ <:speech_balloon:> claudecode ] | ══▸ | () egress <:key:>
  the bubble is quiet — the agent narrates what it did
}
{^"verbose"
  () host | ══▸ | [ <:speaking_head:> claudecode ] | ══▸ | () egress <:key:>
  the head speaks — the agent narrates what it is doing, and why
}
}
  .
  The evidence axis is orthogonal to every other: it re-draws one rune inside the
  square and touches no lane, no dot and no key. Twelve frames above times these
  two is the complete set of twenty-four, without twenty-four near-identical pictures.
}
..
{^"The key has three homes, and the strip is where the operator sees which"
{
{^"at rest — the credentials row not yet touched"
  <:key:> () host | ══▸ | [ claudecode ] | ══▸ | () egress
  the key is yours, on your machine, and has not been handed anywhere
}
{^"forward — it moves INTO the square"
  () host | ══▸ | [ <:key:> claudecode ] | ══▸ | () egress
  the container holds the real value for the whole run, on either backend
}
{^"broker — it stops AT the hop"
  () host | ══▸ | [ claudecode ] | ══▸ | () egress <:key:>
  injected at the hop — proveo's MITM on docker, sbx's own proxy on sbx
}
}
  .
  The key starts beside the host because that is where the secret actually is,
  and the answer to the credentials row is drawn as the place it travels TO. The
  slide from host to its home is the motion that row owns.
}
..
{^"Highlight — the cursor picks what is bright, never what is drawn"
{
{^"cursor on egress — on sbx this row is LOCKED, so the caption says so"
  <color:#9a9a9a>() host</color> | <color:#9a9a9a>══▸</color> | <color:#9a9a9a>[ claudecode ]</color> | **───▸** | **() egress** | **───▸ <:cloud:> <:cloud:>**
}
{^"cursor on credentials or auth"
  <color:#9a9a9a>() host</color> | <color:#9a9a9a>══▸</color> | <color:#9a9a9a>[ claudecode ]</color> | <color:#9a9a9a>══▸</color> | **() egress <:key:>**
}
{^"cursor on execution — greyed AND ticked, so the strip says compulsory"
  <color:#9a9a9a>() host</color> | <color:#9a9a9a>══▸</color> | **[ sbx · claudecode ]** | <color:#9a9a9a>══▸</color> | <color:#9a9a9a>() egress</color>
}
{^"cursor on interface"
  **▴** | **◂──** | **() interface ↑** | <color:#9a9a9a>══▸</color> | <color:#9a9a9a>() egress</color>
}
{^"cursor on agent evidence"
  <color:#9a9a9a>() host</color> | <color:#9a9a9a>══▸</color> | **[ <:speaking_head:> claudecode ]** | <color:#9a9a9a>══▸</color> | <color:#9a9a9a>() egress</color>
}
}
  .
  Every element is present in every frame; the focused row raises its own to bold
  and dims the rest. Nothing appears or vanishes as the operator walks the form,
  so the figure never re-flows under a cursor that is only moving.
  .
  **The dim here is not the form's grey.** In the form, grey means gated off; in
  the strip it means 'not the row you are on'. Two meanings one glyph apart, so
  the strip dims by INTENSITY and keeps colour for the gated case alone.
}
..
{^"The axes that only re-label — same topology, different words in the same cells"
{#
  row | selection | what changes in the strip
  the def being run | claudecode · cursor · opencode · cecli | the square's label, and which variant above applies
  execution | docker (sandbox) — compulsory wherever the harness declares sbx | the square reads 'sbx · <def>'
  execution | docker (dind) — a real toggle, only on a dind harness | the square reads 'dind · <def>', and a daemon glyph joins it
  interface | tui (this session) — always on | the interface dot, always drawn
  interface | + browser | the dot reads 'interface: tui + browser'
  interface | + chrome (host browser) | the return arrow reaches PAST the host dot, to your own Chrome
}
  .
  These re-label; they do not re-shape. Keeping them out of the matrix is what
  holds it at twelve frames, and the strip stays a picture of the three questions
  that actually change the drawing: the backend, the row it puts there, and the key.
  .
  **The lane counts are illustrative, never measured.** A real "how many hosts
  survive" would mean reading the Kit allowlist or Squid's config at prompt time,
  which costs more than the picture is worth — so the counts fall 3, 2, 1 to show
  the axis tightening, and every caption says what the tier DOES rather than
  claiming a number. One lane always survives, because the run has to work.
}
..
{^"Motion — three frames per shape, and the pulse is what carries the meaning"
{
{^"nothing filtered — allow-all, and open — the pulse never slows at the hop"
  f1 | () host | •══▸ | [ def ] | ══▸ | () egress | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  f2 | () host | ══▸ | [ def ] | •══▸ | () egress | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  f3 | () host | ══▸ | [ def ] | ══▸ | () egress | - -•▸ <:cloud:>
}
{^"screened — balanced, and allowlist — one beat at the hop, one lane of three dies"
  f1 | () host | ══▸ | [ def ] | •───▸ | () egress | ───▸ <:cloud:>
  f2 | () host | ══▸ | [ def ] | ───▸ | (•) egress | ───▸ <:cloud:>
  f3 | () host | ══▸ | [ def ] | ───▸ | () egress | ──•▸ <:cloud:> and ───×
}
{^"asked — review — the question walks back up the wire and the agent waits"
  f1 | () host | ══▸ | [ def ] | •══▸ | () egress | <:cloud:>
  f2 | () host | ══▸ | [ def ] | ══▸ | (?) egress | <:cloud:>
  f3 | (?) host ◂─ ─ | ─ ─ | ─ ─ [ def ] | ─ ─ | (?) egress | <:cloud:>
  f4 | () host | ══▸ | [ def ] | ───▸ | () egress | ──▸ <:cloud:>  (you said yes)
}
{^"refused — deny-all — no question, because there is nobody to ask"
  f1 | () host | ══▸ | [ def ] | •───▸ | () egress | ───▸ <:cloud:> Kit
  f2 | () host | ══▸ | [ def ] | ───▸ | (•) egress | ───▸ <:cloud:> Kit
  f3 | () host | ══▸ | [ def ] | ───▸ | () egress | ──•▸ <:cloud:> and ──× the rest
}
}
  .
  Motion is bound to change, not to time: a keystroke runs the filmstrip for
  about 1.2 seconds and the strip then rests on its still frame. An idle prompt
  costs nothing, and any movement means the form just moved.
  .
  **'?' and '×' are different events, so they are different glyphs.** review's
  '?' is a question with somebody to ask: the MITM's CONNECT hook calls the
  reviewgate daemon, which raises a full-screen overlay on the real terminal —
  the same terminal the agent is drawing on, which is why the agent is suspended
  while you answer. That return lane is the whole point of the tier.
  .
  deny-all's '×' has no return lane because there is nothing to ask. It is a
  host-wide baseline with no consent mechanism at all, so a refusal there is the
  end of the story rather than the start of a question — and it refuses
  everything EXCEPT the Kit lane, which is what keeps the provider reachable.
  .
  Two more facts the return lane carries: a decision is CACHED per host for the
  session, so a repeat host never re-asks — and with no tty, or past the
  deadline, the answer defaults to DENY without the overlay ever appearing.
}
}

legend bottom
  **() host · () interface · () egress** — dots: the machine, what the agent drives, the hop
  **the hop is not one thing** — proveo's mitmproxy on docker, sbx's own proxy on sbx
  **a square** — the container boundary; the def name inside it is a label, never a shape
  **<:key:>** — the credential, drawn at the one place it actually rests for the run
  **<:speech_balloon:> / <:speaking_head:>** — agent evidence: default, or verbose
  **<:cloud:>** — the internet: one cloud per lane that survives
  **═══** the session's own traffic · **───** a lane the hop terminates · **- - -** a lane it only watches
  **───×** a lane the policy refuses · **×** — refused, and nobody was asked
  **?** at the hop, with a lane back to () host — review asking YOU, agent suspended
  **bold / dim** — what the cursor's row owns, and everything it does not; NOT the form's gated grey
  a "." cell — element absent, column position preserved for the survivors
end legend
@endsalt
